WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.567
-Our next guest
has his comedy special

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:05.367
"Money Never Wakes"
available on YouTube.

00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:07.901
Please welcome the very funny
Nathan Macintosh.

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:10.033
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:12.567
♪♪

00:00:12.567 --> 00:00:16.167
-Hey. Hey.

00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:17.767
Hey, everybody.

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:22.234
Hi. It's so great to be here.

00:00:22.234 --> 00:00:24.434
Right now I'm trying
to figure my life out.

00:00:24.434 --> 00:00:26.634
Every single person I know
is starting a family.

00:00:26.634 --> 00:00:29.634
I'm losing a lot of friends
to babies.

00:00:29.634 --> 00:00:31.734
I should actually say
I'm losing city friends.

00:00:31.734 --> 00:00:33.067
I'm getting
my small-town friends back

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:34.501
because their kids are now 18.

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:36.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.901
People in small towns
just start families younger.

00:00:37.901 --> 00:00:40.934
Right? And of course they do.
They're bored.

00:00:40.934 --> 00:00:42.267
There's nothing to do
in a small town.

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:44.133
I feel people in a small town
just wake up one day

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:46.734
and look at each other like,
"Look, I don't know.

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:48.267
You want to go see
the trees again?"

00:00:48.267 --> 00:00:49.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:51.968
"We've already seen the trees.

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:54.167
We counted them.
We measured them.

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:56.367
Well, we could make new people
and show them the trees."

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:57.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.901 --> 00:00:59.400
One huge advantage, though,

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:00.834
if you have a baby
in a small town,

00:01:00.834 --> 00:01:03.901
you have space,
you have a house and a yard.

00:01:03.901 --> 00:01:06.234
I have friends in this city
that are having a baby

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:09.133
in a studio apartment,
an apartment

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:10.801
so small that if they
get too many groceries,

00:01:10.801 --> 00:01:12.234
they have to
throw a chair out.

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:14.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.767
The only good thing about
a city apartment

00:01:15.767 --> 00:01:17.501
is your baby
can't just wander off.

00:01:17.501 --> 00:01:18.934
You're not going to lose them.
Like, "Where's Chris?"

00:01:18.934 --> 00:01:21.067
"What do you mean where's Chris?
He's in the West Wing.

00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:23.000
What do you mean where's Chris?

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.934
Our oven and shower touch."

00:01:24.934 --> 00:01:28.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:34.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:34.934 --> 00:01:36.200
I don't know that a lot
of people are taking it.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.100
So everybody wants you
to hold their baby, right?

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.868
Every single person wants you
to hold their baby.

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:42.133
Why? It's the most
precious thing you have.

00:01:42.133 --> 00:01:44.434
Why are you putting it
in my hands?

00:01:44.434 --> 00:01:48.167
People will step over a glass
coffee table covered in candles

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:50.067
to hand you the most
breakable thing they have.

00:01:50.067 --> 00:01:51.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:53.534
Nobody wants you
to touch their phone.

00:01:53.534 --> 00:01:54.767
Not one person.

00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:59.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:02.667
And I honestly don't --
It bothers me.

00:02:02.667 --> 00:02:04.000
I don't think a lot of people
are taking it seriously

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.734
because everybody says they're
having a baby, right?

00:02:05.734 --> 00:02:08.234
Everybody says baby as if that's
all it's ever going to be.

00:02:08.234 --> 00:02:10.100
Babies grow up.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:13.434
I really wish people said
they were having a future adult

00:02:13.434 --> 00:02:14.801
because one day it's a baby

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.734
and the next day
it's a guy named Doug.

00:02:16.734 --> 00:02:19.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.334 --> 00:02:22.934
And Doug is a grown man
standing in your kitchen,

00:02:22.934 --> 00:02:25.334
drinking your juice,
and he wants money.

00:02:25.334 --> 00:02:31.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:31.767 --> 00:02:33.634
There's a lot of people

00:02:33.634 --> 00:02:35.200
that aren't ready
to have a baby, right?

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:38.067
So they get a dog
as a training baby

00:02:38.067 --> 00:02:39.400
and they call it a fur baby.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:42.000
And honest to God,
if you call your dog a fur baby,

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.167
do not have a skin baby
because...

00:02:44.167 --> 00:02:49.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.334 --> 00:02:52.167
You're not taking this
seriously at all.

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:54.234
And having a dog
might be harder sometimes.

00:02:54.234 --> 00:02:57.567
I have a tiny little Chihuahua
and it's horrifying.

00:02:57.567 --> 00:02:59.200
I don't know if anybody's
ever walked a Chihuahua.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:02.467
It's scary.
Walking a Chihuahua is like
walking a carton of eggs.

00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:04.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:09.133
Any single thing can go wrong.

00:03:09.133 --> 00:03:10.934
I got to be on the lookout
for other dogs,

00:03:10.934 --> 00:03:12.767
people, blowing leaves,
everything.

00:03:12.767 --> 00:03:14.067
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.067 --> 00:03:15.968
I don't think people
pushing strollers are worried

00:03:15.968 --> 00:03:17.734
that a hawk is going
to come out of the sky.

00:03:17.734 --> 00:03:19.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.701 --> 00:03:22.033
And take their baby.

00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:24.934
But I have vivid thoughts about
chopping a bird out of the air.

00:03:24.934 --> 00:03:26.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:27.767
Like, "Not today, hawk!"

00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:35.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:35.567 --> 00:03:38.501
I just bought her that sweater,

00:03:38.501 --> 00:03:40.033
which I never thought
I'd ever be doing.

00:03:40.033 --> 00:03:43.367
I never thought I'd be buying
a coat for a tiny little dog.

00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:44.400
I never thought
I'd be in a store

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.701
like, "She'd never wear green,"

00:03:45.701 --> 00:03:47.400
just pushing sweaters
out of the way.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:48.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.701 --> 00:03:50.334
But you have to get clothes
for a Chihuahua

00:03:50.334 --> 00:03:52.934
because if you take a Chihuahua
out in the cold without a coat,

00:03:52.934 --> 00:03:56.067
they freeze.
They stop living right there.

00:03:56.067 --> 00:03:57.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:59.601
And then you're a maniac
just dragging a frozen dog

00:03:59.601 --> 00:04:02.634
down the street. People are
like, "What happened?"

00:04:02.634 --> 00:04:05.234
What happened?
She's supposed to be in Mexico!

00:04:05.234 --> 00:04:09.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:17.667
Also, when you get a dog,

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:19.234
there's so many places
you can't live any more, right?

00:04:19.234 --> 00:04:21.634
Because so many apartments
say no pets,

00:04:21.634 --> 00:04:22.968
and you want to get mad
at the landlord,

00:04:22.968 --> 00:04:24.868
like they're just making up
these crazy rules.

00:04:24.868 --> 00:04:27.033
But people ruined the pets rule

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:28.434
because most people,
when they hear pets,

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:31.300
are like, "Oh, yeah,
a pet, like a cat or a dog."

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:35.100
But some people hear "pets"
and they go, "Oh!

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:36.467
Python."

00:04:36.467 --> 00:04:38.467
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:40.434
And then one day there's
a 40-foot snake

00:04:40.434 --> 00:04:43.834
roaming the halls,
trying to eat your neighbors

00:04:43.834 --> 00:04:46.834
because somebody
doesn't know what a pet is.

00:04:46.834 --> 00:04:49.334
A pet is something
that you can pet.

00:04:49.334 --> 00:04:56.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:56.567 --> 00:04:59.300
You put your hand on its head
and you pet it.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:02.467
It's not a creature you fight
with a stick back into a cage.

00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:03.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.601 --> 00:05:05.567
It's not something you kick
off a riverboat.

00:05:05.567 --> 00:05:07.901
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.901 --> 00:05:10.033
It's not something a wizard
puts on a staff.

00:05:10.033 --> 00:05:12.100
It's --
It's a cute animal with fur.

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:14.300
Not something Samuel L. Jackson
fought on a plane.

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:16.033
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.033 --> 00:05:18.167
There's so many apartments
that say no pets.

00:05:18.167 --> 00:05:20.133
There's not one apartment
that says no babies.

00:05:20.133 --> 00:05:24.100
Not one. And why? My dog is five
pounds for life.

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:25.868
You don't know what
this baby's going to be.

00:05:25.868 --> 00:05:27.367
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.367 --> 00:05:29.434
This baby could grow
into a 6'5" smoker

00:05:29.434 --> 00:05:30.968
that steals packages.
You don't know.

00:05:30.968 --> 00:05:33.100
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:38.667
My dog is doing nothing.
She's sitting there shivering,

00:05:38.667 --> 00:05:40.167
looking out the window for
hawks.

00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:41.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:41.934 --> 00:05:43.133
My name's Nathan Macintosh,
guys.

00:05:43.133 --> 00:05:44.901
Thanks so much.
Really appreciate it.

00:05:44.901 --> 00:05:46.601
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

00:05:46.601 --> 00:05:49.300
-Holy mackerel!
-Thank you, man.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:52.567
-Holy moley!
That's exactly right.

00:05:52.567 --> 00:05:55.868
Standing ovation. That is how
you do it right there.

00:05:55.868 --> 00:05:59.000
Nathan Macintosh.
That is how you do it.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.200
-Appreciate you guys.

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:03.067
-"Money Never Wakes"
is available on YouTube.

00:06:03.067 --> 00:06:05.801
We'll be right back.
That was phenomenal.

